class_name Outfits
## Lookup texture for character.gdshader: everything that differs per job or per tool, read with texelFetch.
## (Big constant arrays indexed per vertex compiled into very slow shaders on Intel/ANGLE: ~10x the GPU time.)
## Layout, 16 RGBA float texels per row:
##   rows 0..39   job looks (data/jobs.json order: 0..30 jobs, 31..35 demons; 39 = no season job). Colors sRGB, -1 = house color.
##     texel 0 shirt.rgb, hat   1 pants.rgb, front   2 hat color.rgb, back   3 front color.rgb, pattern
##     texel 4 back color.rgb, tool (prop index, -1 = by role/track)
##     hats: 0 none 1 helmet 2 crown 3 chef toque 4 straw 5 wizard 6 cap 7 hood 8 bandana 9 mitre 10 top hat 11 turban 12 beret 13 horns
##     front: 0 none 1 apron 2 tabard (house color) 3 tool apron 4 overall bib 5 stole
##     back: 0 none 1 cape 2 satchel 3 quiver 4 backpack 5 mantle; pattern: 0 plain 1 stripes 2 plaid 3 armor 4 robe
##   rows 40..163 tool pieces, 4 per tool (right pole, right head, left pole, left head):
##     texel 0 base.xyz (bottom centre, model space), tilt about Z; texel 1 size.xyz, material
##     tools: 0 none 1 sword 2 daggers 3 shield 4 staff 5 book 6 banner 7 hammer 8 tray 9 shovel 10 spear
##     11 stamp 12 hammer+shield 13 flask 14 needle+cloth 15 gem 16 saw 17 juggling balls 18 crate 19 candle
##     20 mug+rag 21 pan 22 rolling pin 23 flower 24 lute 25 letter 26 fishing rod 27 pickaxe 28 coin bag 29 pitchfork
##     30 demon scythe
##   row 164 material colors (linear): 1 steel 2 wood 3 gold 4 house 5 paper 6 glow 7 red 8 pink 9 green
##     10 dark iron 11 flame 12 white 13 leather
## Regenerate with care: the job order must match chog-hivemind/data/jobs.json.

